# Dev-only defaults. Vite loads this for `npm run dev` and IGNORES it for
# `npm run build`, so production always uses the absolute URL from .env.
#
# Local development talks to a LOCAL backend by default. It used to proxy to
# the production API, which meant every click while testing (approve, publish,
# delete a client) changed real client data.
#
# To work against another API on purpose, put the override in a git-ignored
# `.env.development.local` (Vite loads it after this file), e.g. for staging:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
#   VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=https://staging-api.example.com
#
# Pointing a dev build at the production API still works, but the app then
# shows a red "PRODUCTION API" ribbon on every page. See DevApiWarning.tsx.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=
